## Why This Question Is Asked

Tests the ability to design scalable, highly available job queues with tenant isolation and live rebalancing.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant sharding and hot-tenant handling
- Replica synchronization and consistency models (CP vs AP)
- Online shard rebalancing with lease-based ownership
- Delivery semantics (at-least-once vs exactly-once) and deduplication
- Failure modes, observability, and testing under churn

## Code Example

```javascript
// Acquire shard lease for a tenant
const shardHandle = await acquireShardLease(tenantId);

// Enqueue job to tenant's shard
async function enqueueJob(tenantId, job) {
  const shardId = computeShard(tenantId, job.id);
  const shard = await getShardOwner(shardId);
  return shard.enqueue({ tenantId, job, timestamp: Date.now() });
}

// Idempotent job processing
async function processJob(job, shard) {
  const acquired = await shard.acquireLock(job.id, leaseDuration);
  if (!acquired) return { status: 'skipped' };

  const processed = await checkProcessed(job.id);
  if (processed) return { status: 'duplicate', jobId: job.id };

  await executeJob(job);
  await markProcessed(job.id);
  await shard.releaseLock(job.id);

  return { status: 'completed', jobId: job.id };
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of a beginner-friendly CQRS/event-sourcing workflow with cross-service coordination, compensation patterns, and concrete read model projections.

## Key Concepts

- Append-only EventStore per aggregate root
- Simple saga orchestration with compensation logic
- Read model projection from event streams
- Event-driven communication between bounded contexts

## Code Example

```javascript
// Data contracts
class OrderPlaced { constructor(orderId, items, amount) { this.orderId = orderId; this.items = items; this.amount = amount; } }
class InventoryReserved { constructor(orderId) { this.orderId = orderId; } }
class PaymentAuthorized { constructor(orderId) { this.orderId = orderId; } }
class PaymentFailed { constructor(orderId, reason) { this.orderId = orderId; this.reason = reason; } }
class InventoryRejected { constructor(orderId, reason) { this.orderId = orderId; this.reason = reason; } }

// Append-only EventStore per order
class EventStore {
  constructor() { this.events = new Map(); }
  append(orderId, event) {
    if (!this.events.has(orderId)) this.events.set(orderId, []);
    this.events.get(orderId).push(event);
  }
  getEvents(orderId) { return this.events.get(orderId) || []; }
}

// Saga Orchestrator
class OrderSaga {
  constructor(eventStore, inventoryService, paymentService) {
    this.eventStore = eventStore;
    this.inventory = inventoryService;
    this.payment = paymentService;
  }
  async handle(event) {
    if (event instanceof OrderPlaced) {
      this.eventStore.append(event.orderId, event);
      const inventoryResult = await this.inventory.reserve(event.orderId, event.items);
      if (inventoryResult.success) {
        this.eventStore.append(event.orderId, new InventoryReserved(event.orderId));
        const paymentResult = await this.payment.authorize(event.orderId, event.amount);
        if (paymentResult.success) {
          this.eventStore.append(event.orderId, new PaymentAuthorized(event.orderId));
        } else {
          this.eventStore.append(event.orderId, new PaymentFailed(event.orderId, paymentResult.reason));
          this.compensate(event.orderId);
        }
      } else {
        this.eventStore.append(event.orderId, new InventoryRejected(event.orderId, inventoryResult.reason));
      }
    }
  }
  compensate(orderId) {
    const events = this.eventStore.getEvents(orderId);
    events.reverse().forEach(event => {
      if (event instanceof InventoryReserved) {
        this.inventory.release(orderId);
      }
    });
  }
}

// Read Model Projection
class OrderStatusProjection {
  constructor(eventStore) {
    this.eventStore = eventStore;
    this.orderStatus = new Map();
  }
  project(orderId) {
    const events = this.eventStore.getEvents(orderId);
    let status = 'Pending';
    events.forEach(event => {
      if (event instanceof PaymentAuthorized) status = 'Completed';
      else if (event instanceof PaymentFailed || event instanceof InventoryRejected) status = 'Failed';
    });
    this.orderStatus.set(orderId, status);
    return status;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This question evaluates practical cache invalidation strategies in multi-region Redis deployments, testing understanding of versioned cache keys, cross-region synchronization, and TTL management. It also assesses knowledge of Redis pub/sub versus keyspace notifications and write-through caching trade-offs.

## Key Concepts

- Versioned cache keys with TTL management
- Cross-region invalidation patterns
- Redis pub/sub vs keyspace notifications
- Atomic operations and consistency guarantees
- Write-through vs write-behind caching strategies

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo: bumpVersion(id)
const newVer = await redis.incr(`product:${id}:ver`);
await redis.publish('cache:invalidate', JSON.stringify({id, ver: newVer}));
```

```javascript
// Pseudo: getCache(id)
const currentVer = await redis.get(`product:${id}:ver`);
const cached = await redis.get(`product:${id}:v${currentVer}`);
if (!cached) {
  // Cache miss - refresh from source
  const data = await fetchFromDatabase(id);
  await redis.setex(`product:${id}:v${currentVer}`, 120, JSON.stringify(data));
  return data;
}
return JSON.parse(cached);
```

